  "final_text": "Created a single-point EXCLURAD input file (`input_eta_W1.60_Q2_1.00_cos0.50_phi90.dat`) for the \u03b7-channel with standard CLAS12 settings (EtaMAID model, full O(\u03b1) corrections, 6.53 GeV beam, recoil proton detection, 0.166 GeV\u00b2 inelasticity cut) at W=1.6 GeV, Q\u00b2=1.0 GeV\u00b2, cos\u03b8*=0.5, \u03c6*=90\u00b0.\n\nThis point is physically valid: W=1.6 GeV is well above the p\u03b7 threshold (1.486 GeV) and comfortably inside the EtaMAID-2023 table's W and Q\u00b2 range, and the implied electron kinematics (E'\u22485.1 GeV, \u03b8\u224810\u00b0) are unproblematic. No corrections were needed, so this was written up as a straight `generate`. `outcome.json` documents the choice; since there's no compiler here, I couldn't actually run the executable to get the \u03b4 value."
